    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nAfter enabling `ui2`, in `v` mode, when using `h/l` to move the cursor, some cursors move extra step.\nIt works well without `ui2`\n<img width=\"1462\" height=\"1387\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2a47c34d-1c0d-40a6-a60a-337168c96f31\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```text\naaaaaa\naaaaaa\nbbbbbb\nbbbbbb\ncccccc\ncccccc\n```\n\n1. nvim --clean --noplugin repro.lua\n2. `:lua require(\"vim._core.ui2\").enable()`\n3. `QjjQjjQq=`\n4. `vjlllhhh`\n\nmaybe related? https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41659\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nnot move extra step\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1596+g28ff47b8a4\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\n6.18.26.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nwindows terminal\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nfrom github prerelease download page",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I can reproduce the behavior on Linux as well.\n\nEnvironment:\n- Arch Linux x86_64\n- Neovim: v0.13.0-dev-1623+g8782c70127\n\nThe same behavior occurs as described by the OP.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/baf0d7c9-5a06-4fe5-9c10-5f8ee8cc2842\n\nAdditional note: I can only reproduce this with ui2 enabled. With ui2 disabled, the bug does not occur and the behavior is normal.\n\nThis may indicate that the bug is related to ui2 rather than the operating system.",
